					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MEDIAN\n\nMedian lets you find the middle value from all the given samples. This is not the same as the \"mean\", which is the \"average\" value. Median is the middle value after ordering all the points in the collection.\n\nIn this example we generate 10 random X and Y values for the white circles.\nNext we calculate the median of both X and Y for the red circle.\nAs a result the red circle is always somewhere in the middle\nWe repeated the proces for the average (blue circle)."
					}
				},
